# Secrets — every .env variant except the checked-in template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules/
CLAUDE.md

# Local Claude Code workspace — settings and the security audit record.
# SECURITY_AUDIT.md lives here deliberately: it maps this application's
# weaknesses in detail, which is not something to publish alongside the code.
.claude/

# Build output
client/dist/

# Logs
*.log

# WinSW service binary — a per-host download, not source.
#
# It has to sit in deploy/ because WinSW locates its configuration by matching
# its own filename: homebase-service.exe looks for homebase-service.xml beside
# it. That convention is what puts a ~10MB executable inside a version-
# controlled directory, and the server's install path is itself a git clone.
#
# The .xml IS tracked — it is the configuration and the reason WinSW was chosen
# over NSSM, which hides the same settings in the registry. Only the binary is
# ignored, for the same reason as node_modules/: fetch it per host from
# https://github.com/winsw/winsw/releases rather than trusting a copy in the
# repository. Ignoring it also means `git clean -fd` during a redeploy skips it
# instead of deleting the stopped service's own executable.
deploy/*.exe
deploy/*.exe.config
